Please note that for the last part, the Assert statement is made based on the assumption that the last index of x in the old and new list is different. It's not directly related to the "@@@ last position of x in old and new lists are different". If the comment would mean that the last position of x in old and new lists are different, it would make more sense to compare the old and new count of the array list. The comparison of the old and new indices of x might not be relevant.
