<\code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_index <= New_arrListCount && Old_index >= 0);
<\code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_index);
<\code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX > Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
<\code>
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == true);
<\code>
--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
</code>

This assertion is because the last position of the element `x` in the `arrList` changes when we insert `x` at `index`. The `LastIndexOf` method of `ArrayList` class returns the last index of the specified object in the entire `ArrayList`. If the method returns different values for the same element before and after the insertion, it means that the last position of `x` changed.
